{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1216021-what-supplement-books-are-invaluable-for-the-lore-of-the-setting","id":1216021,"title":"What supplement books are invaluable for the lore of the setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-07T02:45:16-07:00","id":1216021,"title":"What supplement books are invaluable for the lore of the setting?","content":"Hello, for a game I'm planing I was hoping to make it very setting heavy with a focus on the history of the supernaturals. So for my worldbuilding I'm asking for help in seeing what books have interesting setting tidbits that you can't find in the core. The examples I come across is like the Sundered World from Dark Eras with Pangea or the novel Dream of Avarice for mummy. So I'm wondering if there are any other books like that which builds on a splats history? It doesn't necessarily have to be as big as those but something that is interesting lore wise. Also as I'm gonna be buying the first Dark Eras for the stuff on Pangaea I have to ask is there any other Dark Eras in there that also contributes heavily for one or two splat? Anyway what recommendations do you guys have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T03:55:53-07:00","id":1216030,"title":"","content":"Hard to say. The various splat books (for clans, covenants, tribes, orders, etc) all contain lore and history that, unless heavily de-emphasized or explicitly excised as of 2E, are all nice points.<br /> <br /> To The Strongest is another Dark Era that heavily contributes to Mage. It dispels the notion that Mage is about literal descendants of Atlantis or some any other Ancient Magical Civilization, and indeed shows how various mages\u2019 cosmologies and philosophies of King Alexander\u2019s era merged into what we know of today\u2019s Awakened society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T06:07:37-07:00","id":1216070,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Ruined Temple concerns the long history of the Awakened's search for evidence of the Time Before, blasting a hole in the idea that there was a <i>singular</i> Time Before, a singular past the Awakened could find and uncover - the search is as much about the idea of the First City as anything else. It was powerful in shattering the idea of there having been one true Atlantis.<br /> <br /> Dark Eras Companion gives a possible history concerning the origins of the Frankenstein Lineage, and their connection to the Amirani, the Lineage who preceded them. It also has Princes of the Conquered Land, which is useful for a) showing how non-Western cultures interpret the Awakened experience, and b) showing how the splats interpret each others' cosmology (in this case, Mage and Mummy).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T08:42:50-07:00","id":1216152,"title":"","content":"Vampire's clanbooks, and the Ancient books (Ancient Mysteries, Ancient Bloodlines) as well as Requiem for Rome and Fall of the Camarilla. Werewolf has Lore of the Forsaken, Blasphemies, Signs of the Moon and Tribes of the Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T09:51:49-07:00","id":1216185,"title":"","content":"Aside from core books I'd say for Beast Beast Players Guide.<br /> <br /> For Vampire Secrets of the Covenants, Thousand Years of Night, and Half Damned. Spill Blood isn't out yet, but that should have some great lore.<br /> <br /> For Werewolf The Pack and the upcoming Shunned by the Moon.<br /> <br /> For Mage the upcoming Signs of Sorcery (Supernal based mysties), Tome of the Pentacle (Details the history and secrets of the the Orders of the Pentacle), and Fallen World (mysteries of the Fallen World like the Hedge, Underworld, Shadow, Lower Mysteries, and so on), none of which are out yet.<br /> <br /> Promethean perhaps Tormented.<br /> <br /> Changeling Kith and Kin, The Hedge and Changeling Companion should offer lore.<br /> <br /> Dark Eras II should be great for all lines, same with Dark Eras Companion.<br /> <br /> Also I don't recommend anything from 1e as that can change in 2e, alot has.<br /> <br /> In Dark Eras 1 I really only recommend few Eras the rest are 1e or a mechanical mess. The Mage Chapters, The one with the Skin Changers, Browery Dogs (not just for Werewolf IMO Brewery Dogs is great for any gameline period), and the Vampire half of Reqiuem for Regina (but what had been the most usable 2e Changeling Chapter is now useless as the mechanics don't fit the revised Meghan/Rose 2e Changeling, that Chapters 2e was designed for David Hill's version, but if you have the drafts previews it usable and great).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:02:35-07:00","id":1216329,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the recommendations guys. Hopefully these shall be a good read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:44:37-07:00","id":1216347,"title":"","content":"For Mummy, I'd strongly recommend the Book of the Deceived as well as Dreams of Avarice. It goes into pretty deep detail on the history of Irem and the Shan'iatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}